#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mitsub VFD Driver"
msgstr "Controlador VFD Mitsub"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a non-realtime HAL program, written in Python, to control VFDs from Mitsubishi.\n"
"Specifically the A500 F500 E500 A500 D700 E700 F700 series - others may work.\n"
"mitsub_vfd supports serial control using the RS485 protocol.\n"
"Conversion from USB or serial port to RS485 requires special hardware. +"
msgstr ""
"Este es un programa en tiempo no-real escrito en Python para controlar VFDs "
"de Mitsubishi.\n"
"Específicamente las series A500 F500 E500 A500 D700 E700 F700 - otras pueden "
"funcionar.\n"
"mitsub_vfd soporta control serie usando el protocolo RS458.\n"
"La conversión de USB o puerto serie a RS458 requiere hardware especial. +"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:25
msgid ""
"Since this is a non-realtime program it can be affected by computer loading "
"and latency.  It is possible to lose control of the VFDs.  It is optional to "
"set the VFD to stop if it loses communication if that is desirable.  One "
"should always have an Estop circuit that kills the power to the unit in case "
"of emergency."
msgstr ""
"Ya que es un programa en tiempo no-real, puede verse afectado por carga y "
"latencia de la computadora.  Es posible perder el control de los VFDs.  Es "
"opcional configurar el VFD para que se detenga si pierde comunicación, si es "
"deseable.  Uno debería tener siempre un circuito Estop que corte la energía "
"a la unidad en caso de emergencia."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadusr -Wn coolant mitsub_vfd spindle=02 coolant=01\n"
msgstr "loadusr -Wn coolant mitsub_vfd spindle=02 coolant=01\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The above command says:\n"
"loadusr, wait for coolant pins to be ready, component mitsub_vfd, with 2 slaves named spindle (slave #2) and coolant (slave #1)"
msgstr ""
"El comando anterior dice:\n"
"loadusr, espera a que los pines de refrigerante estén listos, componente mitsub_vfd, con 2 esclavos nombrados husillo (esclavo #2) y refrigerante (esclavo #1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:40
msgid "The command line options are:"
msgstr "Las opciones de línea de comandos son:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:42
msgid ""
"'-b or --baud <rate>' : set the baud rate - all networked VFDs must be the "
"same"
msgstr ""
"'-b or --baud <tasa>' : establece la velocidad en baudios - todos los VFDs "
"en red deben usar la misma"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:43
msgid ""
"'-p or --port <device path>' : sets the port to use such as /dev/ttyUSB0"
msgstr ""
"'-p or --port <ruta del dispositivo>' : configura el puerto as usar, como /"
"dev/ttyUSB0"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:44
msgid "'<name>=<slave#>' : sets the HAL component/pin name and slave number."
msgstr ""
"'<nombre>=<#esclavo>' : configura el componente HAL/nombre de pin y número "
"de esclavo."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:46
msgid "Debugging can be toggled by setting the debug pin true."
msgstr ""
"La depuración puede alternarse estableciendo el pin de depuración en "
"Verdadero."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:49
msgid "Turning on debugging will result in a flood of text in the terminal."
msgstr ""
"El activar la depuración resultará en un aluvión de texto en la terminal."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:53
msgid "Where <n> is +mitsub_vfd+ or the name given during loading."
msgstr "Donde <n> es +mitsub_vfd+ o el nombre proporcionado durante la carga."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:56
msgid "'<n>.fwd' (bit, in)  True sets motion forward, False sets reverse."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.fwd' (bit, in)  Verdadero señala movimiento hacia adelante, Falso lo "
"hace en reversa."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:59
msgid "'<n>.run' (bit, in)  True sets the VFD in motion based on the .fwd pin."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.run' (bit, in)  Verdadero pone el VFD en movimiento con base en el pin "
".fwd."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:62
msgid "'<n>.debug' (bit, in)  Prints debug info to the terminal."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.debug' (bit, in)  Imprime información de depuración en la terminal."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:65
msgid "'<n>.alarm' (bit, out)  signals an alarm state of VFD."
msgstr "'<n>.alarm' (bit, out)  Señala un estado de alarma del VFD."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:68
msgid ""
"'<n>.up-to-speed' (bit, out)  when drive is at commanded speed (speed-"
"tolerance is set on vfd)"
msgstr ""
"'<n>.up-to-speed' (bit, out)  Cuando el controlador está a la velocidad "
"ordenada (la tolerancia de velocidad es configurada en el vfd)"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:71
msgid ""
"'<n>.monitor' (bit, in)  some models (eg E500) cannot monitor status - set "
"the monitor pin to false in this case pins such as up-to-speed, amps, alarm "
"and status bits are not updated."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.monitor' (bit, in)  Algunos modelos (p. ej. E500) no pueden monitorear "
"estado (se establece el pin de monitor en Falso) y en este caso los pines "
"como up-to-speed, amps, alarm y status-bit no son actualizados."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:74
msgid ""
"'<n>.motor-cmd' (float, in)  commanded speed to the VFD (scaled to hertz by "
"default)."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.motor-cmd' (float, in)  Velocidad ordenada al VFD (escalada a hertz "
"predeterminadamente)."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:77
msgid ""
"'<n>.motor-fb' (float, out)  feedback speed from the VFD (scaled to hertz by "
"default)."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.motor-fb' (float, out)  Velocidad de retroalimentación del VFD "
"(escalada a hertz predeterminadamente)."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:80
msgid "'<n>.motor-amps' (float, out)  Current amperage output of motor."
msgstr "'<n>.motor-amps' (float, out)  Amperaje de salida actual del motor."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:83
msgid "'<n>.motor-power' (float, out)  Current power output of motor."
msgstr "'<n>.motor-power' (float, out)  Potencia de salida actual del motor."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:86
msgid ""
"'<n>.scale-cmd' (float, in)  Scales the motor-cmd pin to arbitrary units. "
"default 1 = Hertz."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.scale-cmd' (float, in)  Escala el pin motor-cmd a unidades arbitrarias. "
"Predeterminado a 1 = Hertz."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:89
msgid ""
"'<n>.scale-fb' (float, in)  Scales the motor-fb pin to arbitrary units. "
"default 1 = Hertz."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.scale-fb' (float, in)  Escala el pin motor-fb a unidades arbitrarias. "
"Predeterminado a 1 = Hertz."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:92
msgid ""
"'<n>.scale-amps' (float, in)  Scales the motor-amps pin to arbitrary units. "
"default 1 = amps."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.scale-amps' (float, in)  Escala el pin motor-amps a unidades "
"arbitrarias. Predeterminado a 1 = amps."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:95
msgid ""
"'<n>.scale-power' (float, in)  Scales the motor-power pin to arbitrary "
"units. default 1 = ."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.scale-power' (float, in)  Escala el pin motor-power a unidades "
"arbitrarias. Predeterminado a 1 = ."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:98
msgid "'<n>.estop' (bit, in)  puts the VFD into emergency-stopped status."
msgstr "'<n>.estop' (bit, in)  Pone al VFD en estado de parada de emergencia."

#. type: NOTE
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:103
msgid ""
"'<n>.status-bit-N' (bit, out)  N = 0 to 7, status bits are user configurable "
"on the VFD.  Bit 3 should be set to at speed and bit 7 should be set to "
"alarm.  Others are free to be set as required."
msgstr ""
"'<n>.status-bit-N' (bit, out)  N = 0 a 7, los bits de estado son "
"configurables por el usuario en el VFD.  El bit 3 debería configurarse a una "
"velocidad y el bit 7 debería asignarse a una alarma.  Otros son libres de "
"asignación según se requiera."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#\n"
"# example usage of the Mitsubishi VFD driver\n"
"#\n"
"loadusr -Wn coolant mitsub_vfd spindle=02 coolant=01\n"
msgstr ""
"#\n"
"# ejemplo de uso del controlador Mitsubishi VFD\n"
"#\n"
"loadusr -Wn coolant mitsub_vfd spindle=02 coolant=01\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# **************** Spindle VFD setup slave 2 *********************\n"
"net spindle-vel-cmd               spindle.motor-cmd\n"
"net spindle-cw                    spindle.fwd\n"
"net spindle-on                    spindle.run\n"
"net spindle-at-speed              spindle.up-to-speed\n"
"net estop-out                     spindle.estop\n"
"#       cmd scaled to RPM\n"
"setp spindle.scale-cmd .135\n"
"#       feedback is in rpm\n"
"setp spindle.scale-fb 7.411\n"
"#       allows us to see status\n"
"setp spindle.monitor 1\n"
msgstr ""
"# **************** Spindle VFD setup slave 2 *********************\n"
"net spindle-vel-cmd               spindle.motor-cmd\n"
"net spindle-cw                    spindle.fwd\n"
"net spindle-on                    spindle.run\n"
"net spindle-at-speed              spindle.up-to-speed\n"
"net estop-out                     spindle.estop\n"
"#       cmd scaled to RPM\n"
"setp spindle.scale-cmd .135\n"
"#       feedback is in rpm\n"
"setp spindle.scale-fb 7.411\n"
"#       allows us to see status\n"
"setp spindle.monitor 1\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "net spindle-speed-indicator spindle.motor-fb        gladevcp.spindle-speed\n"
msgstr ""
"net spindle-speed-indicator spindle.motor-fb        gladevcp.spindle-speed\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# *************** Coolant vfd setup slave 3 ***********************\n"
"net coolant-flood               coolant.run\n"
"net coolant-is-on               coolant.up-to-speed   gladevcp.coolant-on-led\n"
"net estop-out                   coolant.estop\n"
"#       cmd and feedback scaled to hertz\n"
"setp coolant.scale-cmd 1\n"
"setp coolant.scale-fb 1\n"
"#       command full speed\n"
"setp coolant.motor-cmd 60\n"
"#       allows us to see status\n"
"setp coolant.monitor 1\n"
msgstr ""
"# *************** Coolant vfd setup slave 3 ***********************\n"
"net coolant-flood               coolant.run\n"
"net coolant-is-on               coolant.up-to-speed   gladevcp.coolant-on-"
"led\n"
"net estop-out                   coolant.estop\n"
"#       cmd and feedback scaled to hertz\n"
"setp coolant.scale-cmd 1\n"
"setp coolant.scale-fb 1\n"
"#       command full speed\n"
"setp coolant.motor-cmd 60\n"
"#       allows us to see status\n"
"setp coolant.monitor 1\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuring the Mitsubishi VFD for serial usage"
msgstr "Configuración del VFD Mitsubishi para uso en serie"

#. type: Title ===
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:143 src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:266
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connecting the Serial Port"
msgstr "Conexión del puerto serie"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Mitsubishi VFDs have an RJ-45 jack for serial communication.\n"
"Since they use RS485 protocol,  they can be networked together point to point.\n"
"This driver was tested using the Opto22 AC7A to convert from RS232 to RS485."
msgstr ""
"Los VFDs Mitsubishi tienen un conector RJ-45 para comunicación en serie.\n"
"Dado que usan el protocolo RS485,  pueden ser conectados en red de punto a "
"punto.\n"
"Este controlador ha sido probado con el AC7A de Opto22 para convertir de "
"RS232 a RS485."

#. type: Title ===
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:151 src/drivers/vfs11.adoc:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "Modbus setup"
msgstr "Configuración para Modbus"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:154
msgid "Referenced manuals:"
msgstr "Manuales referenciados:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:157
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'communication option reference manual' and 'A500 technical manual' for 500 series.\n"
"'Fr-A700 F700 E700 D700 technical manual' for the 700 series"
msgstr ""
"'manual de referencia de opciones de comunicación' y 'Manual técnico del "
"A500' para serie 500.\n"
"'Manual técnico de Fr-A700 F700 E700 D700' para la serie 700"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:160
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The VFD must have PR settings adjusted manually for serial communication.\n"
"One must power cycle the VFD for some of these to register eg PR 79"
msgstr ""
"El VFD debe tener configuraciones PR ajustadas manualmente para comunicación "
"en serie.\n"
"Uno debe apagar y prender el VFD para que algunas de ellas sean registradas, "
"p. ej. PR 79"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:163
msgid "'PR 77' set to 1 '-to unlock other PR modification.'"
msgstr "'PR 77' en 1 '-para desbloquear otras modificaciones PR.'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:166
msgid "'PR 79' set to 1 or 0 '-for communication thru serial.'"
msgstr "'PR 79' en 1 o 0 '-para que la comunicación sea por serie .'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:169
msgid ""
"'PR 117' set to 0-31 '-slave number, driver must reference same number.'"
msgstr ""
"'PR 117' entre 0 y 31 '-número de esclavo, el controlador debe referenciar "
"al mimo número.'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:172
msgid ""
"'PR 118' tested with 96 '-baud rate (can be set to 48,96,192) if driver is "
"also set.'"
msgstr ""
"'PR 118' probado con 96 '-velocidad de baudios (puede configurarse a 48, 96, "
"192) si el controlador también lo soporta.'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:175
msgid "'PR 119' set to 0 '-stop bit/data length (8 bits, two stop)'"
msgstr "'PR 119' en 0 '-longitud de bits de paro/datos (8 bits, dos de paro)'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:178
msgid "'PR 120' set to 0 '-no parity'"
msgstr "'PR 120' en 0 '-sin paridad'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:181
msgid "'PR 121' set to 1-10 '-if 10 (maximum) COM errors then VFD faults.'"
msgstr ""
"'PR 121' de 1 a 10 '-Con 10 (máximo) errores de comunicación el VFD falla.'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:184
msgid ""
"'PR 122' tested with 9999 '-if communication is lost VFD will not error.'"
msgstr ""
"'PR 122' probado con 9999 '-si se pierde la comunicación el VFD no emitirá "
"error.'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:187
msgid "'PR 123' set to 9999 '-no wait time is added to the serial data frame.'"
msgstr ""
"'PR 123' en 9999 '-no se agrega tiempo de espera a la trama de datos en "
"serie.'"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/mitsub-vfd.adoc:190
msgid "'PR 124' set to 0 '-no carriage return at end of line.'"
msgstr "'PR 124' en 0 '-sin retorno de carro al final de línea.'"

#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Motenc Driver"
msgstr "Controlador Motenc"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:14
msgid "Vital Systems Motenc-100 and Motenc-LITE"
msgstr "Motenc-100 y Motenc-LITE de Vital Systems"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:22
msgid ""
"The Vital Systems Motenc-100 and Motenc-LITE are 8- and 4-channel servo "
"control boards. The Motenc-100 provides 8 quadrature encoder counters, 8 "
"analog inputs, 8 analog outputs, 64 (68?) digital inputs, and 32 digital "
"outputs. The Motenc-LITE has only 4 encoder counters, 32 digital inputs and "
"16 digital outputs, but it still has 8 analog inputs and 8 analog outputs. "
"The driver automatically identifies the installed board and exports the "
"appropriate HAL objects."
msgstr ""
"Motenc-100 y Motenc-LITE de Vital Systems son placas de servo control de 8 y "
"4 canales. La Motenc-100 proporciona 8 codificadores contadores en "
"cuadratura, 8 entradas analógicas, 8 salidas analógicas, 64 (68?) entradas "
"digitales y 32 salidas digitales. La Motenc-LITE tiene solo 4 codificadores "
"contadores, 32 entradas digitales y 16 salidas digitales, pero también tiene "
"8 entradas analógicas y 8 salidas analógicas. El controlador identifica "
"automáticamente la placa instalada y exporta lo objetos HAL apropiados."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt hal_motenc\n"
msgstr "loadrt hal_motenc\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:34
msgid "Up to 4 boards may be used in one system."
msgstr "En un sistema se pueden usar hasta 4 placas."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:42
msgid ""
"In the following pins, parameters, and functions, <board> is the board ID. "
"According to the naming conventions the first board should always have an ID "
"of zero. However this driver sets the ID based on a pair of jumpers on the "
"board, so it may be non-zero even if there is only one board."
msgstr ""
"En los siguientes pines, parámetros y funciones, <placa> es el identificador "
"de la placa. De acuerdo con las convenciones de nombres, la primera placa "
"debe tener siempre el identificador cero. Sin embargo, este controlador "
"asigna el identificador con base en un par de jumpers en la placa, así que "
"pueden no ser cero incluso si solo hay una placa."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:45
msgid ""
"'(s32) motenc.<board>.enc-<channel>-count' - Encoder position, in counts."
msgstr ""
"'(s32) motenc.<placa>.enc-<canal>-count' - Posición del codificador en "
"conteos."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:47
msgid ""
"'(float) motenc.<board>.enc-<channel>-position' - Encoder position, in user "
"units."
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.enc-<canal>-position' - Posición del codificador, en "
"unidades de usuario."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:49
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.enc-<channel>-index' - Current status of index pulse "
"input."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.enc-<canal>-index' - Estatus actual de la entrada de "
"índice de pulso."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:52
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.enc-<channel>-idx-latch' - Driver sets this pin true "
"when it latches an index pulse (enabled by latch-index). Cleared by clearing "
"latch-index."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.enc-<canal>-idx-latch' - El controlador establece este "
"pin en Verdadero cuando enclava un pulso de índice (activado por latch-index)"
". Se apaga cuando latch-index es Falso."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:54
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.enc-<channel>-latch-index' - If this pin is true, the "
"driver will reset the counter on the next index pulse."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.enc-<canal>-latch-index' - Si este pin es Verdadero el "
"controlador restablecerá el contador en el siguiente pulso de índice."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:57
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.enc-<channel>-reset-count' - If this pin is true, the "
"counter will immediately be reset to zero, and the pin will be cleared."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.enc-<canal>-reset-count' - Si este pin es Verdadero, "
"el contador será restablecido inmediatamente a cero, y el pin será limpiado."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:59
msgid ""
"'(float) motenc.<board>.dac-<channel>-value' - Analog output value for DAC "
"(in user units, see -gain and -offset)"
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.dac-<canal>-value' - Valor de salida analógica para "
"DAC (en unidades de usuario, ver -gain y -offset)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:61
msgid ""
"'(float) motenc.<board>.adc-<channel>-value' - Analog input value read by "
"ADC (in user units, see -gain and -offset)"
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.adc-<canal>-value' - Valor de la entrada analógica "
"leída por el ADC (en unidades de usuario, ver -gain y -offset)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:63
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.in-<channel>' - State of digital input pin, see "
"canonical digital input."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.in-<canal>' - Estado del pin de entrada digital, ver "
"entrada digital canónica."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:65
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.in-<channel>-not' - Inverted state of digital input "
"pin, see canonical digital input."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.in-<canal>-not' - Estado invertido del pin de entrada "
"digital, ver entrada digital canónica."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:67
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.out-<channel>' - Value to be written to digital "
"output, seen canonical digital output."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.out-<canal>' - Valor a ser escrito en la salida "
"digital, ver salida digital canónica."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:69
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.estop-in' - Dedicated estop input, more details needed."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.estop-in' - Entrada dedicada estop, se necesitan más "
"detalles."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:71
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.estop-in-not' - Inverted state of dedicated estop "
"input."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.estop-in-not' - Estado invertido de la entrada "
"dedicada estop."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:73
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.watchdog-reset' - Bidirectional, - Set TRUE to reset "
"watchdog once, is automatically cleared."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.watchdog-reset' - Bidireccional, - Verdadero para "
"restablecer el perro guardián una vez, es limpiado automáticamente."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:78
msgid ""
"'(float) motenc.<board>.enc-<channel>-scale' - The number of counts / user "
"unit (to convert from counts to units)."
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.enc-<canal>-scale' - El número de conteos / unidades "
"de usuario (para convertir conteos a unidades)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:80
msgid "'(float) motenc.<board>.dac-<channel>-offset' - Sets the DAC offset."
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.dac-<canal>-offset' - Establece la compensación de "
"DAC."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:82
msgid ""
"'(float) motenc.<board>.dac-<channel>-gain' - Sets the DAC gain (scaling)."
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.dac-<canal>-gain' - Establece la ganancia de DAC "
"(escalamiento)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:84
msgid "'(float) motenc.<board>.adc-<channel>-offset' - Sets the ADC offset."
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.adc-<canal>-offset' - Establece la compensación de "
"ADC."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:86
msgid ""
"'(float) motenc.<board>.adc-<channel>-gain' - Sets the ADC gain (scaling)."
msgstr ""
"'(float) motenc.<placa>.adc-<canal>-gain' - Establece la ganancia de ADC "
"(escalamiento)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:88
msgid ""
"'(bit) motenc.<board>.out-<channel>-invert' - Inverts a digital output, see "
"canonical digital output."
msgstr ""
"'(bit) motenc.<placa>.out-<canal>-invert' - Invierte una salida digital, ver "
"salida digital canónica."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'(u32) motenc.<board>.watchdog-control' - Configures the watchdog.\n"
"The value may be a bitwise OR of the following values:"
msgstr ""
"'(u32) motenc.<placa>.watchdog-control' - Configura el perro guardián.\n"
"El valor puede ser un OR de los siguientes bits:"

#. type: Table
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bit #"
msgstr "No. de bit"

#. type: Table
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:95 src/gcode/overview.adoc:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "Significado"

#. type: Table
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Timeout is 16ms if set, 8ms if unset"
msgstr "El tiempo límite es de 16ms si es activo, 8ms si es inactivo"

#. type: Table
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "Watchdog is enabled"
msgstr "El perro guardián está activo"

#. type: Table
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "Watchdog is automatically reset by DAC writes (the HAL dac-write function)"
msgstr ""
"El perro guardián se restablece automáticamente con escrituras DAC (la "
"función dac-write de HAL)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:104
msgid ""
"Typically, the useful values are 0 (watchdog disabled) or 20 (8ms watchdog "
"enabled, cleared by dac-write)."
msgstr ""
"Típicamente, los valores útiles son 0 (perro guardián inactivo) o 20 (8ms, "
"perro guardián activo, limpiado por dac-write)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:107
msgid "'(u32) motenc.<board>.led-view' - Maps some of the I/O to onboard LEDs."
msgstr ""
"'(u32) motenc.<placa>.led-view' - Mapea algunas de las E/S a los LEDs de la "
"placa."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:112
msgid "'(funct) motenc.<board>.encoder-read' - Reads all encoder counters."
msgstr ""
"'(funct) motenc.<placa>.encoder-read' - Lee todos los codificadores "
"contadores."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:114
msgid ""
"'(funct) motenc.<board>.adc-read' - Reads the analog-to-digital converters."
msgstr ""
"'(funct) motenc.<placa>.adc-read' - Lee los convertidores analógico-digital."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:116
msgid "'(funct) motenc.<board>.digital-in-read' - Reads digital inputs."
msgstr "'(funct) motenc.<placa>.digital-in-read' - Lee entradas digitales."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:118
msgid "'(funct) motenc.<board>.dac-write' - Writes the voltages to the DACs."
msgstr "'(funct) motenc.<placa>.dac-write' - Escribe los voltajes en los DACs."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:120
msgid "'(funct) motenc.<board>.digital-out-write' - Writes digital outputs."
msgstr "'(funct) motenc.<placa>.digital-out-write' - Escribe salidas digitales."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/motenc.adoc:122
msgid "'(funct) motenc.<board>.misc-update' - Updates misc stuff."
msgstr "'(funct) motenc.<placa>.misc-update' - Actualiza los misceláneos."

#. type: Title =
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Opto22 Driver"
msgstr "Controlador Opto22"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:14
msgid "*PCI AC5 ADAPTER CARD / HAL DRIVER*"
msgstr "*TARJETA ADAPTADORA PCI AC5 / CONTROLADOR HAL*"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Adapter Card"
msgstr "La tarjeta adaptadora"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:25
msgid ""
"This is a card made by Opto22 for adapting the PCI port to solid state relay "
"racks such as their standard or G4 series. It has 2 ports that can control "
"up to 24 points each and has 4 on board LEDs. The ports use 50 pin "
"connectors the same as Mesa boards. Any relay racks/breakout boards that "
"work with Mesa Cards should work with this card with the understanding any "
"encoder counters, PWM, etc., would have to be done in software. The AC5 does "
"not have any 'smart' logic on board, it is just an adapter."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una tarjeta hecha por Opto22 para adaptar el puerto PCI a racks de "
"relevadores en estado sólido como sus series standard y G4. Tiene 2 puertos "
"que pueden controlar hasta 24 puntos cada uno y tiene 4 LEDs en la placa. "
"Los puertos usan conectores de 50 pines iguales que las placas Mesa. "
"Cualquier placa de relevador(es) individual/en rack que funcione con "
"tarjetas Mesa debería funcionar con esta tarjeta bajo el entendido de que "
"cualquier codificador contador, PWM, etc. debe ocurrir en el software. La "
"AC5 no tiene ninguna lógica 'inteligente' en la placa, es solo un adaptador."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:27
msgid "See the manufacturer's website for more info:"
msgstr "Vea el sitio web del fabricante para mayor información:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:29
msgid "https://www.opto22.com/site/pr_details.aspx?cid=4&item=PCI-AC5"
msgstr "https://www.opto22.com/site/pr_details.aspx?cid=4&item=PCI-AC5"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:32
msgid ""
"I would like to thank Opto22 for releasing info in their manual, easing the "
"writing of this driver!"
msgstr ""
"Quisiera agradecer a Opto22 por divulgar la información de su manual que "
"facilitó la escritura de este controlador!"

#. type: Title ==
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Driver"
msgstr "El controlador"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:39
msgid ""
"This driver is for the PCI AC5 card and will not work with the ISA AC5 card. "
"The HAL driver is a realtime module. It will support 4 cards as is (more "
"cards are possible with a change in the source code). Load the basic driver "
"like so:"
msgstr ""
"Este controlador es para la tarjeta PCI AC5 y no funcionará con la tarjeta "
"ISA AC5. El controlador HAL es un módulo en tiempo real. Soportará 4 "
"tarjetas tal cual (se pueden más tarjetas cambiando el código fuente). "
"Cargue el controlador básico así:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "loadrt opto_ac5\n"
msgstr "loadrt opto_ac5\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:50
msgid ""
"This will load the driver which will search for max 4 boards. It will set I/"
"O of each board's 2 ports to a default setting. The default configuration is "
"for 12 inputs then 12 outputs. The pin name numbers correspond to the "
"position on the relay rack. For example the pin names for the default I/O "
"setting of port 0 would be:"
msgstr ""
"Esto cargará el controlador, el cual buscará hasta 4 placas. Configurará E/S "
"de los 2 puertos de cada placa predeterminadamente, la cual es para 12 "
"entradas y 12 salidas. Los números de nombre de pines corresponden a la "
"posición en el rack de relevadores. Por ejemplo, los nombres de pines para "
"las configuración predeterminada de E/S del puerto 0 será:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:53
msgid "'opto_ac5.0.port0.in-00' - They would be numbered from 00 to 11"
msgstr "'opto_ac5.0.port0.in-00' - Serán numerados del 00 al 11"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:55
msgid ""
"'opto_ac5.0.port0.out-12' - They would be numbered 12 to 23 port 1 would be "
"the same."
msgstr ""
"'opto_ac5.0.port0.out-12' - Serán numerados de 12 al 23, lo mismo para el "
"puerto 1."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:59
msgid "'opto_ac5.[BOARDNUMBER].port[PORTNUMBER].in-[PINNUMBER] OUT bit' -"
msgstr "'opto_ac5.[PLACA].port[PUERTO].in-[PIN] OUT bit' -"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:66
msgid ""
"'opto_ac5.[BOARDNUMBER].port[PORTNUMBER].in-[PINNUMBER]-not OUT bit' - "
"Connect a HAL bit signal to this pin to read an I/O point from the card. The "
"PINNUMBER represents the position in the relay rack. Eg.  PINNUMBER 0 is "
"position 0 in a Opto22 relay rack and would be pin 47 on the 50 pin header "
"connector. The -not pin is inverted so that LOW gives TRUE and HIGH gives "
"FALSE."
msgstr ""
"'opto_ac5.[PLACA].port[PUERTO].in-[PIN]-not OUT bit' - Conecta una señal bit "
"de HAL a este pin para leer un punto de E/S de la tarjeta. El PIN representa "
"la posición en el rack de relevadores. P. ej. PIN 0 es la posición 0 en un "
"rack de relevadores Opto22 y sería el pin 47 en el conector de 50 pines. El "
"pin -not está invertido, así que Bajo da Verdadero y Alto da Falso."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:72
msgid ""
"'opto_ac5.[BOARDNUMBER].port[PORTNUMBER].out-[PINNUMBER] IN bit' - Connect a "
"HAL bit signal to this pin to write to an I/O point of the card. The "
"PINNUMBER represents the position in the relay rack.Eg.  PINNUMBER 23 is "
"position 23 in a Opto22 relay rack and would be pin 1 on the 50 pin header "
"connector."
msgstr ""
"'opto_ac5.[PLACA].port[PUERTO].out-[PIN] IN bit' - Conecta una señal bit de "
"HAL a este pin para escribir a un punto de E/S de la tarjeta. El PIN "
"representa la posición en el rack de relevadores. P. ej. PIN 23 es la "
"posición 23 en un rack de relevadores Opto22 y sería el pin 1 en el conector "
"de 50 pines."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:75
msgid ""
"'opto_ac5.[BOARDNUMBER].led[NUMBER] OUT bit' - Turns one of the 4 onboard "
"LEDs on/off. LEDs are numbered 0 to 3."
msgstr ""
"'opto_ac5.[PLACA].led[NÚMERO] OUT bit' - Enciende/Apaga uno de los 4 LEDs en "
"la placa. Los LEDs están numerados del 0 al 3."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:78
msgid ""
"BOARDNUMBER can be 0-3 PORTNUMBER can be 0 or 1. Port 0 is closest to the "
"card bracket."
msgstr ""
"PLACA puede ser 0-3, PUERTO puede ser 0 o 1. El puerto 0 es el más cercano "
"al soporte de la tarjeta."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/drivers/opto22.adoc:84
msgid ""
"'opto_ac5.[BOARDNUMBER].port[PORTNUMBER].out-[PINNUMBER]-invert W bit' - "
"When TRUE, invert the meaning of the corresponding -out pin so that TRUE "
"gives LOW and FALSE gives HIGH."
msgstr ""
"'opto_ac5.[PLACA].port[PUERTO].out-[PIN]-invert W bit' - Cuando es Verdadero "
"invierte el sentido del -out pin correspondiente, de tal manera que "
"Verdadero da Bajo y Falso da Alto."

