#. type: Title ===
#: src/gui/gladevcp.adoc:495
#, no-wrap
msgid "Python attributes and methods of HAL Widgets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gladevcp.adoc:500
msgid ""
"HAL widgets are instances of GtKWidgets and hence inherit the methods, "
"properties and signals of the applicable GtkWidget class.  For instance, to "
"figure out which GtkWidget-related methods, properties and signals a "
"'HAL_Button' has, lookup the description of https://lazka.github.io/pgi-docs/"
"#Gtk-3.0/classes/Button.html#Gtk.Button[GtkButton] in the https://"
"lazka.github.io/pgi-docs/[PyGObject API Reference]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gladevcp.adoc:504
msgid ""
"An easy way to find out the inheritance relationship of a given HAL widget "
"is as follows: Run glade, place the widget in a window, and select it; then "
"choose the 'Signals' tab in the 'Properties' window.  For example, selecting "
"a 'HAL_LED' widget, this will show that a 'HAL_LED' is derived from a "
"'GtkWidget', which in turn is derived from a 'GtkObject', and eventually a "
"'GObject'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gladevcp.adoc:507
msgid ""
"Full class hierarchy can be seen by invoking the GtkInspector while in the "
"Glade GUI by selecting a widget then pressing Control-Shift-I.  If the "
"Inspector doesn't open then it can be enabled from a terminal by entering:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/gladevcp.adoc:509
#, no-wrap
msgid "gsettings set org.gtk.Settings.Debug enable-inspector-keybinding true\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/gladevcp.adoc:511
msgid ""
"The Inspector is also handy for testing css style changes \"on the fly\" as "
"well as determining all the properties and signals available for a widget."
msgstr ""

