#. type: Title ==
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:448
#, no-wrap
msgid "Class Patch The File Manager Widget"
msgstr "Parchear la clase del widget administrador de archivos"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:455
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Class patching (monkey patching) is a little like _black magic_ - so use it _only when needed_. The Major problem is if the widget library functions are changed during development, the functions may break.\n"
"The File manager widget is designed to load a selected program in LinuxCNC.\n"
"But maybe you want to print the file name first."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:464
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can \"class patch\" the library to _redirect the function call_.\n"
"You can do this class patch inside or outside the HandlerClass instance.\n"
"This will change what 'self' represents in the function.\n"
"Outside the HanderClass, 'self' will be the patched class instance.\n"
"Inside the HanderClass, 'self' will be the HandlerClass instance.\n"
"This would change what functions/variables you can access in the function.\n"
"Here we show an inside the HandlerClass example:\n"
"In the `IMPORT SECTION` add:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:468
#, no-wrap
msgid "from qtvcp.widgets.file_manager import FileManager as FM\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:471
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here we are going to:"
msgstr "Hay dos tipos de números:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:473
msgid "_Keep a reference to the original function_ (1) so we can still call it"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:474
msgid ""
"_Redirect the class to call our custom function_ (2) in the handler file "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:480
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"##########################################\n"
"# Special Functions called from QtVCP    #\n"
"##########################################\n"
msgstr ""
"###########################################\n"
"# **** INSTANTIATE LIBRARIES SECTION **** #\n"
"###########################################\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:486
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# For changing functions in widgets we can 'class patch'.\n"
"# class patching must be done before the class is instantiated.\n"
"def class_patch__(self):\n"
"    self.old_load = FM.load # keep a reference of the old function <1>\n"
"    FM.load = self.our_load # redirect function to our handle file function <2>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:494
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Write a custom function to replace the original_:\n"
"This function must have the *same signature as the original function*.\n"
"'self' is the HandlerClass instance _not_ the patched class instance.\n"
"In this example we are still going to call the original function by using the reference to it we recorded earlier.\n"
"It _requires the first argument to be the widget instance_, which in this case is `self.w.filemanager` (the name given in the Qt Designer editor)."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-code-snippets.adoc:504
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def our_load(self,fname):\n"
"    print(fname)\n"
"    self.old_load(self.w.filemanager,fname)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
