#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2520
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Register to `STATUS` channel*:\n"
"To set this up, first register to catch the `general` message from `STATUS`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2531
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Add a function to call a dialog*:\n"
"This function must _build a message `dict` to send to the dialog_.\n"
"This message will be passed back in the general message with the addition of the _`return` variable_.\n"
"It is possible to add _extra user information_ to the message. The dialog will ignore these and pass them back."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2531
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NAME`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2532
msgid "Launches code name of dialog to show."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2532
#, no-wrap
msgid "`ID`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2533
msgid "A unique id so we process only a dialog that we requested."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2533
#, no-wrap
msgid "`TITLE`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2534
msgid "The title to use on the dialog."
msgstr "El título a usar en el diálogo."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2542
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def show_dialog(self):\n"
"    mess = {'NAME':'ENTRY','ID':'__test1__',\n"
"            'TITLE':'Test Entry'}\n"
"    ACTION.CALL_DIALOG, mess)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2548
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Add a callback function that processes the general message*:\n"
"Keep in mind this function will _get all general messages_ so the `dict` keynames are not guaranteed to be there. Using the `.get()` function and/or using `try`/`except` is advisable. This function should:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2549
msgid "check the name and id is the same as we sent,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2550
msgid "then extract the return value and any user variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/gui/qtvcp-widgets.adoc:2561
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# process the STATUS return message\n"
"def return_value(self, w, message):\n"
"    rtn = message.get('RETURN')\n"
"    code = bool(message.get('ID') == '__test1__')\n"
"    name = bool(message.get('NAME') == 'ENTRY')\n"
"    if code and name and not rtn is None:\n"
"        print('Entry return value from {} = {}'.format(code, rtn))\n"
msgstr ""

