#. type: Title ===
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:532
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "sincos"
msgstr "sincos"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:537
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This component computes the sine and cosine of an input angle in radians.  "
"It has different capabilities than the \"sine\" and \"cosine\" outputs of "
"siggen, because the input is an angle, rather than running freely based on a "
"\"frequency\" parameter."
msgstr ""
"Este componente calcula el seno y el coseno de un ángulo en radianes. Tiene "
"diferentes capacidades que las salidas \"seno\" y \"coseno\" de siggen, "
"porque la entrada es un ángulo, en lugar de correr libremente basado en un "
"parámetro de \"frecuencia\"."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:540
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The pins are declared with the names 'sin_' and 'cos_' in the source code so "
"that they do not interfere with the functions 'sin()' and 'cos()'.  The HAL "
"pins are still called 'sincos.<num>.sin'."
msgstr ""
"Los pines se declaran con los nombres 'sin_' y 'cos_' en el código fuente "
"para que no interfieran con las funciones 'sin()' y 'cos()'. Los pines HAL, "
"sin embargo, se llaman 'sincos.<num>.sin'."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:553
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"component sincos;\n"
"pin out float sin_;\n"
"pin out float cos_;\n"
"pin in float theta;\n"
"option period no;\n"
"function _;\n"
"license \"GPL\"; // indicates GPL v2 or later\n"
";;\n"
"#include <rtapi_math.h>\n"
"FUNCTION(_) { sin_ = sin(theta); cos_ = cos(theta); }\n"
msgstr ""
"component sincos;\n"
"pin out float sin_;\n"
"pin out float cos_;\n"
"pin in float theta;\n"
"option period no;\n"
"function _;\n"
"license \"GPL\"; // indica GPL v2 o posterior\n"
";;\n"
"#include <rtapi_math.h>\n"
"FUNCTION(_) { sin_ = sin(theta); cos_ = cos(theta); }\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:555
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "out8"
msgstr "out8"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:561
msgid ""
"This component is a driver for a 'fictional' card called \"out8\", which has "
"8 pins of digital output which are treated as a single 8-bit value.  There "
"can be a varying number of such cards in the system, and they can be at "
"various addresses.  The pin is called 'out_' because 'out' is an identifier "
"used in '<asm/io.h>'.  It illustrates the use of 'EXTRA_SETUP' and "
"'EXTRA_CLEANUP' to request an I/O region and then free it in case of error "
"or when the module is unloaded."
msgstr ""
"Este componente es un controlador para una tarjeta 'ficticia' llamada "
"\"out8\", que tiene 8 pines de salida digital que son tratado como un solo "
"valor de 8 bits.  Puede haber un número variable de tales tarjetas en el "
"sistema, y pueden estar en varias direcciones.  El pin es llamado 'out_' "
"porque 'out' es un identificador utilizado en '<asm/io.h>'.  Eso ilustra el "
"uso de 'EXTRA_SETUP' y 'EXTRA_CLEANUP' para solicitar una región de E/S y "
"luego liberarla en caso de error o cuando el módulo sea descargado."

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:567
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"component out8;\n"
"pin out unsigned out_ \"Output value; only low 8 bits are used\";\n"
"param r unsigned ioaddr;\n"
msgstr ""
"component out8;\n"
"pin out unsigned out_ \"Valor de salida, solo se usan los 8 bits mas bajos\";\n"
"param r unsigned ioaddr;\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/hal/comp.adoc:569
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "function _;\n"
msgstr "function _;\n"

