#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:14
msgid "*elbpcom* [_common options_] _HEXDATA_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Read or write data from a Mesa ethernet card that uses the LBP16 protocol, "
"such as the 7I80. This can be useful for performing certain low-level tasks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:24
msgid ""
"For more information about the meaning of each address space, see the card "
"documentation.  Incorrect use of this utility can have negative effects such "
"as changing the board's IP address or even corrupting the FPGA bitfile in "
"the EEPROM.  For some tasks, such as updating FPGA bitfiles and setting IP "
"addresses, *mesaflash*(1) is a more appropriate tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:26
msgid "If not specified, the default values are"
msgstr "Si no se especifican, los valores predeterminados son"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:28
msgid ""
"**--ip=**_192.168.1.121_ **--port=**_27181_ **--timeout=**_.2_ **--"
"space=**_0_ **--size=**_0_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:31
msgid ""
"If the **--size** argument _TRANSFER_SIZE_ is 0, elbpcom will look up the "
"preferred transfer size of the space in the space's info area."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:33
msgid ""
"This example demonstrates reading the HOSTMOT2 identifying string from the "
"IDROM in space 0:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ elbpcom --address 0x104 --read 8\n"
"> 82420401\n"
"< 484f53544d4f5432\n"
"      HOSTMOT2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:44
msgid ""
"First the request is shown in hex. Then the response (if any) is shown in "
"hex.  Finally, the response is shown in ASCII, with \".\" replacing any non-"
"ASCII characters.  This is similar to the following invocations of mesaflash:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ ./mesaflash  --device 7i80 --rpo 0x104\n"
"54534F48\n"
"$ ./mesaflash  --device 7i80 --rpo 0x108\n"
"32544F4D\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:53
msgid "Notice its different treatment of byte order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/elbpcom.1.adoc:57
msgid ""
"mesaflash(1), hostmot2(9), hm2_eth(9), https://www.mesanet.com[Mesa's "
"documentation for the Anything I/O boards]."
msgstr ""

