#, no-wrap
msgid "USAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:52
msgid ""
"Normal usage is to load the component in your HAL file and net the "
"appropriate pins from the__ motion__ and__ io__ components.  The following "
"lines are typical in a HAL file when using the hal_manualtoolchange non-"
"realtime component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:53
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*loadusr -W hal_manualtoolchange*"
msgstr "Cambio manual de herramienta"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:56
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This will load the hal_manualtoolchange non-realtime component waiting for "
"the component to be ready before continuing."
msgstr ""
"initialize_manual_toolchange (self): permite una renovación completa del "
"manual sistema de cambio de herramientas."

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`net tool-change iocontrol.0.tool-change => hal_manualtoolchange.change`*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:62
msgid ""
"When an M6 code is run, motion sets _iocontrol.0.tool-change_ to high "
"indicating a tool change. This pin should be netted to "
"_hal_manualtoolchange.change_. This causes the Tool change dialog to be "
"displayed on screen and wait for the user to either click the continue "
"button on the dialog or press an externally connected button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`net tool-changed iocontrol.0.tool-changed <= hal_manualtoolchange.changed`*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:68
msgid ""
"When the Tool change dialog's continue button is pressed, it will set the "
"_hal_manualtoolchange.changed_ pin to high, this should be netted to the "
"_iocontrol.0.tool-changed_ pin, indicating to the motion controller that the "
"tool change has been completed and can continue with the execution of the G-"
"code program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`net tool-number iocontrol.0.tool-prep-number => hal_manualtoolchange.number`*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:74
msgid ""
"When a _T-_ command is executed in a G-code program, the tool number will "
"held in the _iocontrol.0.tool-prep-number_. This pin should be netted to "
"_hal_manualtoolchange.number_. The value of this pin, the tool number is "
"displayed in the tool change dialog to let the user know which tool should "
"be loaded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "*`net tool-prepare-loopback iocontrol.0.tool-prepare => iocontrol.0.tool-prepared`*"
msgstr "*`net tool-prepare-loopback iocontrol.0.tool-prepare => iocontrol.0.tool-prepared`*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:79
msgid ""
"The _iocontrol.0.tool-prepare_ pin will go true when a T__n__ tool prepare "
"is requested. Since there is not automated tool changer this pin should be "
"netted to _iocontrol.0.tool-prepared_ to indocate that the tool has been "
"prepared."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:85
msgid ""
"If you wish to use an external button to signal the hal_manualtoolchange "
"component that the tool change is complete simply bring the button into HAL "
"(via a parport input pin or a hostmot2 gpio input or similar), and wire it "
"directly to the _hal_manualtoolchange.change_button_ pin. For Example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "net tool-changed-btn hal_manualtoolchange.change_button <= parport.0.pin-15-in\n"
msgstr "net tool-changed-btn hal_manualtoolchange.change_button <= parport.0.pin-15-in\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/hal_manualtoolchange.1.adoc:92
msgid "motion(1), iocontrol(1), halcmd(1)."
msgstr ""

