#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "halmeter(1)"
msgstr "halmeter(1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:6
msgid "halmeter - observe HAL pins, signals, and parameters"
msgstr "halmeter - observa pines, señales y parámetros de HAL"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:10
msgid ""
"*halmeter* [*-s*] [**pin**|**sig**|**param** _name_] [*-g* _X-position Y-"
"position_ [_Width_]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:17
msgid ""
"The tool *halmeter* is used to observe HAL (Hardware Abstraction Layer) "
"pins, signals, or parameters. It serves the same purpose as a multimeter "
"does when working on physical systems. It is an self-contained application "
"and connects independently to HAL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:20
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*pin* _name_"
msgstr "<nombre-específico>"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:22
msgid "Display the HAL pin _name_."
msgstr "Muestra el pin HAL _nombre_."

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:22
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*sig* _name_"
msgstr "get_name"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:24
msgid "Display the HAL signal _name_."
msgstr "Muestra la señal HAL _nombre_."

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "*param* _name_"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:26
msgid "Display the HAL parameter _name_."
msgstr "Muestra el parámetro HAL _nombre_."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:29
msgid ""
"If neither *pin*, *sig*, or *param* are specified, the window starts out "
"blank and the user must select an item to observe:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:35
msgid ""
"Small window. Non-interactive, must be used with *pin*, *sig*, or *param* to "
"select the item to display. The item name is displayed in the title bar "
"instead of the window, and there are no \"Select\" or \"Exit\" buttons. "
"Handy when you want a lot of meters in a small space."
msgstr ""
"Ventana pequeña. No interactiva, debe usarse con *pin*, *sig*, o *param* "
"para seleccionar el elemento a mostrar. El nombre del elemento se muestra en "
"la barra de título en vez de la ventana, y no hay botones \"Select\" o "
"\"Exit\". Útil cuando se quieren varios medidores en un espacio pequeño."

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-g*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Geometry position. Allows one to specify the initial starting position and "
"optionally the width of the meter. Referenced from top left of screen in "
"pixel units. Handy when you want to load a lot of meters in a script with "
"out them displaying on top of each other."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:46
msgid ""
"Unless *\\-s* is specified, there are two buttons, \"Select\" and \"Exit\".  "
"\"Select\" opens a dialog box to select the item (pin, signal, or parameter) "
"to be observed. \"Exit\" does what you expect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:51
msgid ""
"The selection dialog has \"OK\", \"Apply\", and \"Cancel\" buttons. OK "
"displays the selected item and closes the dialog. \"Apply\" displays the "
"selected item but keeps the selection dialog open. \"Cancel\" closes the "
"dialog without changing the displayed item."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:52 src/man/man1/rs274.1.adoc:33
#: src/man/man1/sendkeys.1.adoc:93 src/man/man1/sim_pin.1.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "*halmeter*"
msgstr "*halmeter*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:58
msgid ""
"Opens a meter window, with nothing initially displayed. Use the \"Select\" "
"button to choose an item to observe. Does not return until the window is "
"closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "*halmeter &*"
msgstr "*halmeter &*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:62
msgid ""
"Open a meter window, with nothing initially displayed. Use the \"Select\" "
"button to choose an item. Runs in the background leaving the shell free for "
"other commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "*halmeter pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *&*"
msgstr "*halmeter pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *&*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:65
msgid ""
"Open a meter window, initially displaying HAL pin _parport.0.pin-03-out_.  "
"The \"Select\" button can be used to display other items. Runs in background."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "*halmeter -s pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *&*"
msgstr "*halmeter -s pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *&*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:68
msgid ""
"Open a small meter window, displaying HAL pin _parport.0.pin-03-out_.  The "
"displayed item cannot be changed. Runs in background."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "*halmeter -s pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *-g* _100 500_ *&*"
msgstr "*halmeter -s pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *-g* _100 500_ *&*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:72
msgid ""
"Open a small meter window, displaying HAL pin _parport.0.pin-03-out_.  "
"places it 100 pixels to the left and 500 pixels down from top of screen. The "
"displayed item cannot be changed. Runs in background."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "*halmeter -s pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *-g* _100 500 400_ *&*"
msgstr "*halmeter -s pin* _parport.0.pin-03-out_ *-g* _100 500 400_ *&*"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halmeter.1.adoc:77
msgid ""
"Open a small meter window, displaying HAL pin _parport.0.pin-03-out_.  "
"places it 100 pixels to the left and 500 pixels down from top of screen. The "
"width will be 400 pixels (270 is default) The displayed item cannot be "
"changed. Runs in background."
msgstr ""

