#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:21
msgid ""
"The convenience script *halrun* can manipulate the HAL (Hardware Abstraction "
"Layer) from the command line. When invoked, *halrun*:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:23
msgid "Sets up the realtime environment."
msgstr "Configura el ambiente de tiempo real."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:24
msgid "Executes a command interpreter (*halcmd* or *haltcl*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:25
msgid "(Optionally) runs an interactive session."
msgstr "(Opcionalmente) ejecuta un sesión interactiva."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:26
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tears down the realtime environment."
msgstr "Carga de componentes de tiempo real."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:29
msgid ""
"If no filename is specified, an interactive session is started.  The session "
"will use *halcmd*(1) unless *-T* is specified in which case *haltcl*(1) will "
"be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:34
msgid ""
"If a filename is specified and neither the *-I* nor the *-T* option is "
"included, the filename will be processed by the command interpreter "
"corresponding to the filename extension (*halcmd* or *haltcl*).  After "
"processing, the realtime environment will be torn down."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:38
msgid ""
"If a filename is specified and the *-I* or *-T* option is included, the file "
"is processed by the appropriate command interpreter and then an interactive "
"session is started for *halcmd* or *haltcl* according to the *-I* or *-T* "
"option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:41
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*halcmd_opts*"
msgstr "Halscope"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:45
msgid ""
"When a .hal file is specified, the *halcmd_opts* are passed to *halcmd*.  "
"See the man page for **halcmd**(1).  When a .tcl file is specified, the only "
"valid options are: -i <INI file> -f <filename[.tcl|.hal]> (alternate means "
"of specifying a file)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:47
msgid "Run an interactive *halcmd* session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "*-T*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man1/halrun.1.adoc:49
msgid "Run an interactive *haltcl* session."
