#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:37
msgid ""
"hm2_7i43 is a device driver that interfaces the Mesa 7i43 board with the "
"HostMot2 firmware to the LinuxCNC HAL. Both the 200K and the 400K FPGAs are "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:42
msgid ""
"The driver talks with the 7i43 over the parallel port, not over USB. USB can "
"be used to power the 7i43, but not to talk to it. USB communication with the "
"7i43 will not be supported any time soon, since USB has poor real-time "
"qualities."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:47
msgid ""
"The driver programs the board's FPGA with firmware when it registers the "
"board with the hostmot2 driver. The firmware to load is specified in the "
"*config* modparam, as described in the hostmot2(9) manpage, in the _config "
"modparam_ section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:48
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Jumper settings"
msgstr "Configuración ini "

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:53
msgid ""
"To send the FPGA configuration from the PC, the board must be configured to "
"get its firmware from the EPP port. To do this, jumpers W4 and W5 must both "
"be down, ie toward the USB connector."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:56
msgid ""
"The board must be configured to power on whether or not the USB interface is "
"active.  This is done by setting jumper W7 up, ie away from the edge of the "
"board."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:57 src/man/man9/hm2_7i90.9.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "Communicating with the board"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:61
msgid ""
"The 7i43 communicates with the LinuxCNC computer over EPP, the Enhanced "
"Parallel Port.  This provides about 1 Mbps of throughput, and the "
"communication latency is very predictable and reasonably low."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:65 src/man/man9/hm2_7i90.9.adoc:53
msgid ""
"The parallel port must support EPP 1.7 or EPP 1.9. EPP 1.9 is preferred, but "
"EPP 1.7 will work too. The EPP mode of the parallel port is sometimes a "
"setting in the BIOS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:69
msgid ""
"Note that the popular \"NetMOS\" aka \"MosChip 9805\" PCI parport cards *do "
"not work*.  They do not meet the EPP spec, and cannot be reliably used with "
"the 7i43.  You have to find another card, sorry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:75
msgid ""
"EPP is very reliable under normal circumstances, but bad cabling or "
"excessively long cabling runs may cause communication timeouts.  The driver "
"exports a parameter named `hm2_7i43.<BoardNum>.io_error` to inform HAL of "
"this condition.  When the driver detects an EPP timeout, it sets io_error to "
"True and stops communicating with the 7i43 board.  Setting io_error back to "
"False makes the driver start trying to communicate with the 7i43 again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/hm2_7i43.9.adoc:77 src/man/man9/hm2_7i90.9.adoc:68
msgid ""
"Access to the EPP bus is not threadsafe: only one realtime thread may access "
"the EPP bus."
msgstr ""

