#. type: Title =
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:1
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "stepgen(9)"
msgstr "stepgen"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:6
msgid "stepgen - software step pulse generation"
msgstr "stepgen - generación de pulsos a pasos por software"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:10
msgid ""
"**loadrt stepgen step_type=**_type0_[,_type1_...] "
"[**ctrl_type=**_type0_[,_type1_...]] [**user_step_type=#,#**...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:17
msgid ""
"*stepgen* is used to control stepper motors. The maximum step rate depends "
"on the CPU and other factors, and is usually in the range of 5 kHz to 25 "
"kHz. If higher rates are needed, a hardware step generator is a better "
"choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:28
msgid ""
"*stepgen* has two control modes, which can be selected on a channel by "
"channel basis using *ctrl_type*. Possible values are \"*p*\" for position "
"control, and \"*v*\" for velocity control. The default is position control, "
"which drives the motor to a commanded position, subject to acceleration and "
"velocity limits. Velocity control drives the motor at a commanded speed, "
"again subject to accel and velocity limits. Usually, position mode is used "
"for machine axes. Velocity mode is reserved for unusual applications where "
"continuous movement at some speed is desired, instead of movement to a "
"specific position. (Note that velocity mode replaces the former component "
"*freqgen*.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:34
msgid ""
"*stepgen* can control a maximum of 16 motors. The number of motors/channels "
"actually loaded depends on the number of _type_ values given. The value of "
"each _type_ determines the outputs for that channel.  Position or velocity "
"mode can be individually selected for each channel.  Both control modes "
"support the same 16 possible step types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:39
msgid ""
"By far the most common step type is '0', standard step and direction.  "
"Others include up/down, quadrature, and a wide variety of three, four, and "
"five phase patterns that can be used to directly control some types of motor "
"windings. (When used with appropriate buffers of course.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:43
msgid ""
"Some of the stepping types are described below, but for more details "
"(including timing diagrams) see the *stepgen* section of the HAL reference "
"manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "type 0: step/dir"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:51
msgid ""
"Two pins, one for step and one for direction. *make-pulses* must run at "
"least twice for each step (once to set the step pin true, once to clear it). "
"This limits the maximum step rate to half (or less) of the rate that can be "
"reached by types 2-14. The parameters *steplen* and *stepspace* can further "
"lower the maximum step rate. Parameters *dirsetup* and *dirhold* also apply "
"to this step type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "type 1: up/down"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:54
msgid ""
"Two pins, one for 'step up' and one for 'step down'. Like type 0, *make-"
"pulses* must run twice per step, which limits the maximum speed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "type 2: quadrature"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:57
msgid ""
"Two pins, phase-A and phase-B. For forward motion, A leads B. Can advance by "
"one step every time *make-pulses* runs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "type 3: three phase, full step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:61
msgid ""
"Three pins, phase-A, phase-B, and phase-C. Three steps per full cycle, then "
"repeats. Only one phase is high at a time - for forward motion the pattern "
"is A, then B, then C, then A again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "type 4: three phase, half step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:65
msgid ""
"Three pins, phases A through C. Six steps per full cycle. First A is high "
"alone, then A and B together, then B alone, then B and C together, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "types 5 through 8: four phase, full step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:71
msgid ""
"Four pins, phases A through D. Four steps per full cycle. Types 5 and 6 are "
"suitable for use with unipolar steppers, where power is applied to the "
"center tap of each winding, and four open-collector transistors drive the "
"ends. Types 7 and 8 are suitable for bipolar steppers, driven by two H-"
"bridges."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "types 9 and 10: four phase, half step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:74
msgid ""
"Four pins, phases A through D. Eight steps per full cycle. Type 9 is "
"suitable for unipolar drive, and type 10 for bipolar drive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "types 11 and 12: five phase, full step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:77
msgid ""
"Five pins, phases A through E. Five steps per full cycle. See HAL reference "
"manual for the patterns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "types 13 and 14: five phase, half step"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:80
msgid ""
"Five pins, phases A through E. Ten steps per full cycle. See HAL reference "
"manual for the patterns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:80
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "type 15: user-specified"
msgstr "el número R no está especificado"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:83
msgid ""
"This uses the waveform specified by the *user_step_type* module parameter, "
"which may have up to 10 steps and 5 phases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "*stepgen.make-pulses* (no floating-point)"
msgstr "*stepgen.make-pulses* (sin punto flotante)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:90
msgid ""
"Generates the step pulses, using information computed by *update-freq*.  "
"Must be called as frequently as possible, to maximize the attainable step "
"rate and minimize jitter.  Operates on all channels at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "*stepgen.capture-position* (uses floating point)"
msgstr "*stepgen.capture-position* (usa punto flotante)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:93
msgid ""
"Captures position feedback value from the high speed code and makes it "
"available on a pin for use elsewhere in the system.  Operates on all "
"channels at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "*stepgen.update-freq* (uses floating point)"
msgstr "*stepgen.update-freq* (usa punto flotante)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:96
msgid ""
"Accepts a velocity or position command and converts it into a form usable by "
"*make-pulses* for step generation.  Operates on all channels at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "**stepgen.**__N__**.counts** s32 out"
msgstr "**stepgen.**__N__**.counts** s32 out"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/man/man9/stepgen.9.adoc:101
msgid ""
"The current position, in counts, for channel _N_. Updated by *capture-"
"position*."
msgstr ""

