#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:177
msgid ""
"Only one of either *Float Switch* or *Ohmic Probe* is required. If both are "
"used, then *Float Switch* will be a fallback if *Ohmic Probe* is not sensed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:179
msgid ""
"If *Ohmic Probe* is used, then *Ohmic Probe Enable* is required to be "
"checked on the QtPlasmaC GUI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:182
msgid ""
"*Breakaway Switch* is not mandatory because the *Float Switch* is treated "
"the same as a breakaway when not probing.  If they are two separate "
"switches, and there are not enough inputs on the breakout board, they could "
"be combined and connected as a *Float Switch*."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:187
msgid ""
"The minimum I/O requirement for a QtPlasmaC configuration to function are: "
"*Arc Voltage* input OR *Arc OK* input, *Float Switch* input, and *Torch On* "
"output.  To reiterate, in this case QtPlasmaC will treat the float switch as "
"a breakaway switch when it is not probing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recommended Settings:"
msgstr "Configuración recomendada:"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:192
msgid ""
"Refer to the <<plasma:initial-setup,Heights Diagrams>> for a visual "
"representation of the terms below."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:196
msgid ""
"*[AXIS_Z] MIN_LIMIT* should be just below top of the slats with allowances "
"for float_switch_travel and over travel tolerance.  For example, if the "
"user's float switch takes 4 mm (0.157\") to activate then set the Z minimum "
"to 5 mm (0.2\")  plus an allowance for overrun (either calculated using the "
"equation below or allow 5 mm (0.2\") below the lowest slat)."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:197
msgid ""
"*[AXIS_Z] MAX_LIMIT* should be the highest the user wants the Z axis to "
"travel (it must not be lower than Z HOME_OFFSET)."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:198
msgid ""
"*[AXIS_Z] HOME* should be set to be approximately 5 mm-10 mm (0.2\"-0.4\") "
"below the maximum limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:200
msgid ""
"*Floating Head* - it is recommended that a floating head be used and that it "
"has enough movement to allow for overrun during probing.  Overrun can be "
"calculated using the following formula:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:203
#, no-wrap
msgid "o = 0.5 * a * (v / a)^2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:206
msgid ""
"where: o = overrun, a = acceleration in units/s^2^ and v = velocity in units/"
"s."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:208
msgid ""
"Metric example: given a Z axis MAX_ACCELERATION of 600 mm/s^2^ and "
"MAX_VELOCITY of 60 mm/s, the overrun would be 3 mm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:210
msgid ""
"Imperial example: given a Z axis MAX_ACCELERATION of 24 in/s^2^ and "
"MAX_VELOCITY of 2.4 in/s, the overrun would be 0.12 in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:213
msgid ""
"On machines that will utilize an ohmic probe as the primary method of "
"probing, it is highly recommended to install a switch on the floating head "
"as a backup means of stopping Z motion in the event of ohmic probe failure "
"due to dirty surfaces."
msgstr ""

