#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1722
#, no-wrap
msgid "Path Tolerance"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1725
msgid ""
"Path tolerance is set with a G64 command and a following P value. The P "
"value corresponds to the amount that the actual cut path followed by the "
"machine may deviate from the programmed cut path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1727
msgid ""
"The default LinuxCNC path tolerance is set for maximum speed which will "
"severely round corners when used with normal plasma cutting speeds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1729
msgid ""
"It is recommended that the path tolerance is set by placing the appropriate "
"G64 command and P value in the header of each G-code file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1733
msgid ""
"The provided G-code filter program will test for the existence of a `G64 "
"P__n__` command prior to the first motion command.  If no G64 command is "
"found it will insert a `G64 P0.1` command which sets the path tolerance to "
"0.1 mm.  For a imperial config the command will be `G64 P0.004`."
msgstr ""

