#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1873
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Velocity Based THC*"
msgstr "*THC basado en velocidad*"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1877
msgid ""
"If the cut velocity falls below a percentage of *CutFeedRate* (as defined by "
"the VAD Threshold % value in the THC frame of the CONFIGURATION section of "
"the <<plasma:parameters-tab,PARAMETERS Tab>>) the THC will be locked until "
"the cut velocity returns to at least 99.9% of *CutFeedRate*.  This will be "
"made apparent by the *VELOCITY ANTI DIVE* indicator illuminating in the "
"<<plasma:control-panel,CONTROL Panel>> on the <<plasma:main-tab,MAIN Tab>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1879
msgid ""
"Velocity based THC prevents the torch height being changed when velocity is "
"reduced for a sharp corner or a small hole."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1881
msgid ""
"It is important to note that <<plasma:velocity-reduction,Velocity "
"Reduction>> affects the Velocity Based THC in the following ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1883
msgid ""
"If Velocity Reduction is invoked in the middle of the cut, the THC will be "
"locked."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1884
msgid ""
"The THC will remain locked until the velocity reduction is canceled by "
"returning it to a value that is above the *VAD Threshold*, and the torch "
"actually reaches 99.9% of the *CutFeedRate*."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1890
msgid ""
"LinuxCNC (QtPlasmaC) has the ability to automatically adjust the cut path of "
"the current program by the amount specified in Kerf Width of the selected "
"material's Cut Parameters.  This is helpful if the G-code is programmed to "
"the nominal cut path and the user will be running the program on different "
"thickness materials to help ensure consistently sized parts."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1892
msgid ""
"To use cutter compensation the user will need to use G41.1, G42.1 and G40 "
"with the kerf width HAL pin:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1894
msgid ""
"`G41.1 D#<_hal[plasmac.kerf-width]>` : offsets torch to the left of the "
"programmed path"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1895
msgid ""
"`G42.1 D#<_hal[plasmac.kerf-width]>` : offsets torch to the right of the "
"programmed path"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1896
msgid "`G40` turns the cutter compensation off"
msgstr "`G40` desactiva la compensación del cortador"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1898
msgid ""
"IF *CUTTER COMPENSATION* IS IN EFFECT *G-CODE THC*, *VELOCITY BASED THC* AND "
"*OVER CUT* ARE NOT ABLE TO BE USED; AN ERROR MESSAGE WILL BE DISPLAYED."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1900
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Initial Height Sense (IHS) Skip"
msgstr "Detección de altura inicial"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1903
msgid "Initial Height Sense may be skipped in one of two different ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1906
msgid ""
"If the THC is disabled, or the THC is enabled but not active, then the IHS "
"skip will occur if the start of the cut is less than *Skip IHS* distance "
"from the last successful probe."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1907
msgid ""
"If the THC is enabled and active, then the IHS skip will occur if the start "
"of the cut is less than *Skip IHS* distance from the end of the last cut."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1909
msgid "A value of zero for *Skip IHS* will disable all IHS skipping."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1911
msgid ""
"Any errors encountered during a cut will disable IHS skipping for the next "
"cut if *Skip IHS* is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1918
msgid ""
"Probing may be done with either ohmic sensing or a float switch.  It is also "
"possible to combine the two methods, in which case the float switch will "
"provide a fallback to ohmic probing.  An alternative to ohmic probing is "
"<<plasma:offset_probing,Offset Probing>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1922
msgid ""
"If the machine's torch does not support ohmic probing, the user could have a "
"separate probe next to the torch.  In this case the user would extend the "
"probe below the torch.  The probe must NOT extend more than the minimum Cut "
"Height below the torch and the Z axis offset distance needs to be entered as "
"the *Ohmic Offset* in the PROBING frame of the CONFIGURATION section of the "
"<<plasma:parameters-tab,PARAMETERS Tab>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1924
msgid ""
"Probing setup is done in the PROBING frame of the CONFIGURATION section of "
"the <<plasma:parameters-tab,PARAMETERS Tab>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1927
msgid ""
"QtPlasmaC can probe at the full Z axis velocity so long as the machine has "
"enough movement in the float switch to absorb any overrun.  If the machine's "
"float switch travel is suitable, the user could set the Probe Height to near "
"the Z axis MINIMUM_LIMIT and do all probing at full speed."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1929
msgid ""
"Some float switches can exhibit a large switching hysteresis which shows up "
"in the probing sequence as an excessive time to complete the final probe up."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1931
msgid "This time may be decreased by changing the speed of the final probe up."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1932
msgid "This speed defaults to 0.001 mm (0.000039\") per servo cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1933
msgid ""
"It is possible to increase this speed by up to a factor of 10 by adding the "
"following line to the custom.hal file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1937
#, no-wrap
msgid "setp plasmac.probe-final-speed n\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1940
msgid ""
"where _n_ is a value from 1-10. It is recommended to keep this value as low "
"as possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1942
msgid ""
"Using this feature will change the final height slightly and will require "
"thorough probe testing to confirm the final height."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1944
msgid ""
"This speed value affects ALL probing so if the user uses ohmic probing and "
"the user changes this speed value then the user will need to probe test to "
"set the require offset to compensate for this speed change as well as the "
"float travel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1946
msgid ""
"The reliability of this feature will only be as good as the repeatability of "
"the float switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1949
msgid "Probe Height refers to the height above the Z axis MINIMUM_LIMIT."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1951
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Offset Probing"
msgstr "5: Probing"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1956
msgid ""
"Offset Probing is the use of a probe that is offset from the torch.  This "
"method is an alternative to Ohmic Probing and uses the `plasmac.ohmic-"
"enable` output pin to operate a solenoid for extending and retracting the "
"probe.  The `plasmac.ohmic-probe` input pin is used to detect the material "
"and the *Ohmic Offset* in the PROBING frame of the CONFIGURATION section of "
"the <<plasma:parameters-tab,PARAMETERS Tab>> is used to set the correct "
"measured height."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1959
msgid ""
"The probe could be a mechanically deployed probe, a permanently mounted "
"proximity sensor or even simply a stiff piece of wire extending about 0.5 mm "
"(0.2\") below the torch tip.  If the probe is mechanically deployed, then it "
"needs to extend/retract rather quickly to avoid excessive probing times and "
"would commonly be pneumatically operated."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1961
msgid ""
"To use this feature, the user must set the probe's offset from the torch "
"center by following the procedure described in <<peripheral-"
"offsets,Peripheral Offsets>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1963
msgid ""
"To modify the offsets manually, the user could edit either or both the "
"following options in the *[OFFSET_PROBING]* section of the "
"_<machine_name>_.prefs file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1969
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"X axis = n.n\n"
"Y axis = n.n\n"
"Delay = t.t\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1972
msgid ""
"where _n.n_ is the offset of the probe from the torch center in machine "
"units for the X and Y axes and _t.t_ is the time in seconds to allow for any "
"mechanical deployment of the probe if required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1974
msgid ""
"Each of these parameters is optional and also may appear in any order. If a "
"parameter is not detected, then the default is 0.0. There can be no space "
"after the X or Z, lower case is permissible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1977
msgid ""
"When this variable appears in the _<machine_name>_.prefs file with either X "
"or Y not equal to zero, then QtPlasmaC will do *all* Ohmic Probing as Offset "
"Probing.  If Offset Probing is valid then the feed rate at which the X and Y "
"axes move to the offset position may be adjusted by the use of the *Offset "
"Speed* parameter in the PROBING frame of the <<plasma:parameters-"
"tab,PARAMETERS Tab>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1979
msgid ""
"When a probe sequence has begun, the `plasmac.ohmic-enable` pin will be set "
"True causing the probe to extend. When the material is detected the "
"`plasmac.ohmic-enable` pin will be reset to false causing the probe to "
"retract."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1982
msgid ""
"The probe will begin moving to the offset position simultaneously with the Z "
"axis moving down to the Probe Height, probing will not commence unless the "
"deployment timer has completed.  It is required that the *Probe Height* in "
"the PROBING frame of the CONFIGURATION section of the <<plasma:parameters-"
"tab,PARAMETERS Tab>> is above the top of the material to ensure that the "
"probe is fully offset to the correct X/Y position before the final vertical "
"probe down movement."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1984
msgid ""
"PROBE HEIGHT NEEDS TO BE SET ABOVE THE TOP OF THE MATERIAL FOR OFFSET "
"PROBING."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1986
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Cut Types"
msgstr "Tipo"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1989
msgid "QtPlasmaC allows two different cut modes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1991
#, fuzzy
msgid "*NORMAL CUT* - runs the loaded G-code program to pierce then cut."
msgstr "Ejecute el programa."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1992
msgid ""
"<<plasma:pierce-only,*PIERCE ONLY*>> - only pierces the material at each cut "
"start position, useful prior to a *NORMAL CUT* on <<plasma:thick-"
"materials,thick materials>>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1994
#, fuzzy
msgid "There are two ways of enabling this feature:"
msgstr "Hay dos tipos de números:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1996
msgid ""
"Utilize the default <<plasma:button-cut,custom user button>> to toggle "
"between the cut types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:1997
msgid ""
"Adding the following line to the G-code program before the first cut to "
"enable *Pierce Only* mode for the current file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2001
#, no-wrap
msgid "#<pierce-only> = 1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2004
msgid ""
"If using a custom user button is utilized then QtPlasmaC will automatically "
"reload the file when the cut type is toggled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2005
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hole Cutting - Intro"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2008
msgid ""
"It is recommended that any holes to be cut have a diameter no less than one "
"and a half times the thickness of the material to be cut."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2010
msgid ""
"It is also recommended that holes with a diameter of less than 32&#8239;mm "
"(1.26\") are cut at 60% of the feed rate used for profile cuts. This should "
"also lock out THC due to velocity constraints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2012
msgid ""
"QtPlasmaC can utilize G-code commands usually set by a CAM Post Processor "
"(PP) to aid in hole cutting or if the user does not have a PP or the user's "
"PP does not support these methods then QtPlasmaC can automatically adapt the "
"G-code to suit. This automatic mode is disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2014
msgid ""
"There are three methods available for improving the quality of small holes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2016
msgid ""
"*Velocity Reduction* - <<plasma:hole-cutting-velocity-reduction,Reducing the "
"velocity>> to approximately 60% of the *CutFeedRate*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2017
msgid ""
"*Arc Dwell (<<plasma:pause-at-end,Pause At End>>)* - Keeping the torch on "
"for a short time at the end of the hole while motion is stopped to allow the "
"arc to catch up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2018
msgid ""
"*Over cut* - Turning the torch off at the end of the hole then continue "
"along the path."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2021
msgid ""
"If both *Arc Dwell* and *Over cut* are active at the same time, then *Over "
"cut* will take precedence."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2023
msgid ""
"*OVER CUT* IS NOT ABLE TO BE USED IF CUTTER COMPENSATION IS IN EFFECT; AN "
"ERROR MESSAGE WILL BE DISPLAYED."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2024
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Hole Cutting"
msgstr "Modo de corte de espuma"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2027
msgid ""
"G-code commands can be set up by either by a CAM Post Processor (PP) or by "
"hand coding."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2029
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*Hole Cutting Velocity Reduction*"
msgstr "Resolucion del monitor"

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2034
msgid ""
"If cutting a hole requires a reduced velocity, then the user would use the "
"following command to set the velocity: `M67 E3 Qnn` where `nn` is the "
"percentage of the velocity desired.  For example, `M67 E3 Q60` would set the "
"velocity to 60% of the current material's *CutFeedRate*."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2037
msgid ""
"In order to use this feature, LinuxCNC's Adaptive Feed Control (M52) must be "
"turned on (P1).  This is also a requirement for <<plasma:paused-"
"motion,Paused Motion>> during <<plasma:cut-recovery,Cut Recovery>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2039
msgid ""
"To enable *Hole Cutting Velocity Reduction* The preamble of the G-code must "
"contain the following line:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2046
msgid ""
"To turn off *Hole Cutting Velocity Reduction* at any point, use the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2053
msgid "See the <<plasma:velocity_thc,Velocity Based THC>> section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2054
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample code for hole cutting with reduced velocity."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2070
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"G21 (metric)\n"
"G64 P0.005\n"
"M52 P1 (enable adaptive feed)\n"
"F#<_hal[plasmac.cut-feed-rate]> (feed rate from cut parameters)\n"
"G0 X10 Y10\n"
"M3 $0 S1 (start cut)\n"
"G1 X0\n"
"M67 E3 Q60 (reduce feed rate to 60%)\n"
"G3 I10 (the hole)\n"
"M67 E3 Q0 (restore feed rate to 100%)\n"
"M5 $0 (end cut)\n"
"G0 X0 Y0\n"
"M2 (end job)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2072 src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2151
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "*Arc Dwell (Pause At End)*"
msgstr "Movimientos Z"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2075
msgid ""
"This method can be invoked by setting the <<plasma:pause-at-end,Pause At "
"End>> parameter in the MATERIAL frame of the <<plasma:parameters-"
"tab,PARAMETERS Tab>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2077 src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2142
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Over cut*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2081
msgid ""
"The torch can be turned off at the end of the hole by setting the "
"`motion.digital-out-03` pin with the M-Codes `M62` (Synchronized with "
"Motion)* or `M64` (Immediate).  After turning the torch off it is necessary "
"to allow the torch to be turned on again before beginning the next cut by "
"resetting the `motion.digital-out-03` pin with the M-Codes `M63` or `M65`, "
"this will be done automatically by the QtPlasmaC G-code parser if it reaches "
"an M5 command without seeing a `M63 P3` or `M65 P3`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2083
msgid ""
"After the torch is turned off the hole path will be followed for a default "
"length of 4 mm (0.157\"). This distance may be specified by adding "
"`#<oclength> =` _n_ to the G-code file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2085
msgid "`M62 P3` will turn the torch off (Synchronized with Motion)"
msgstr "`M62 P3` apagará la antorcha (Sincronizado con movimiento)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2086
msgid ""
"`M63 P3` will allow the torch to be turned on (Synchronized with Motion)"
msgstr "`M63 P3` permitirá encender la antorcha (Sincronizado con movimiento)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2087
msgid "`M64 P3` will turn the torch off (Immediately)"
msgstr "`M64 P3` apagará la antorcha (Inmediatamente)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2088
msgid "`M65 P3` will allow the torch to be turned on (Immediately)"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2090 src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2295
msgid ""
"It is important to thoroughly understand the difference between "
"*Synchronized with motion* and *Immediate*:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2093
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`M62 and M63` (Synchronized with Motion) - The actual change of the "
"specified output (P2 (THC) for example) will happen at the beginning of the "
"next motion command.  If there is no subsequent motion command, the output "
"changes will not occur. It is best practice to program a motion code (G0 or "
"G1 for example) right after a M62 or M63."
msgstr ""
"El cambio real de las salidas especificadas ocurrirá en el comienzo del "
"siguiente comando de movimiento. Si no hay movimiento posterior, los cambios "
"de salida en cola no sucederán. Lo mejor es siempre programar un código G de "
"movimiento (G0, G1, etc.) justo después del M62/63."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2095
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`M64 and M65` (Immediate) - These commands happen immediately as they are "
"received by the motion controller. Since these are not synchronized with "
"motion, they will break blending.  This means if these codes are used in the "
"middle of active motion codes, the motion will pause to activate these "
"commands."
msgstr ""
"La salida M68 ocurre inmediatamente cuando son recibidos por el controlador. "
"No están sincronizados con el movimiento, y harán romper la mezcla. M68 "
"funciona igual que M64-65."

#. type: Block title
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2097 src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample code:"
msgstr "Código de muestra:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2116
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"G21 (metric)\n"
"G64 P0.005\n"
"M52 P1 (enable adaptive feed)\n"
"F#<_hal[plasmac.cut-feed-rate]> (feed rate from cut parameters)\n"
"G0 X10 Y10\n"
"M3 $0 S1 (start cut)\n"
"G1 X0\n"
"M67 E3 Q60 (reduce feed rate to 60%)\n"
"G3 I10 (the hole)\n"
"M62 P3 (turn torch off)\n"
"G3 X0.8 Y6.081 I10 (continue motion for 4 mm)\n"
"M63 P3 (allow torch to be turned on)\n"
"M67 E3 Q0 (restore feed rate to 100%)\n"
"M5 $0 (end cut)\n"
"G0 X0 Y0\n"
"M2 (end job)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2119
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hole Cutting - Automatic"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2122
msgid ""
"QtPlasmaC has the ability to automatically modify the G-code to reduce the "
"velocity and/or apply *Over cut* which can be useful when cutting holes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2124
msgid ""
"For valid hole sensing it is required that all values in the G2 or G3 G-code "
"line are explicit, an error dialog will be displayed if any values are "
"mathematically calculated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2126
msgid ""
"QtPlasmaC Hole Sensing is disabled by default. It can be enabled/disabled by "
"using the following G-code parameters to select the desired hole sensing "
"mode:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2128
msgid ""
"`#<holes> = 0` - Causes QtPlasmaC to disable hole sensing if it was "
"previously enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2129
msgid ""
"`#<holes> = 1` - Causes QtPlasmaC to reduce the speed of holes less than 32 "
"mm (1.26\") to 60% of *CutFeedRate*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2130
msgid ""
"`#<holes> = 2` - Causes QtPlasmaC to <<plasma:overcut,Over cut>> the hole in "
"addition to the velocity changes in setting 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2131
msgid ""
"`#<holes> = 3` - Causes QtPlasmaC to reduce the speed of holes less than 32 "
"mm (1.26\") and arcs less than 16 mm (0.63\") to 60% of *CutFeedRate*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2132
msgid ""
"`#<holes> = 4` - Causes QtPlasmaC to <<plasma:overcut,Over cut>> the hole in "
"addition to the velocity change in setting 3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2134
msgid ""
"The default hole size for QtPlasmaC hole sensing is 32&#8239;mm (1.26\"). It "
"is possible to change this value with the following command in a G-code file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2136
msgid ""
"`#<h_diameter> =` _nn_ - To set a diameter (_nn_) in the same units system "
"as the rest of the G-code file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2139
msgid ""
"The default velocity for QtPlasmaC small holes is 60% of the current feed "
"rate.  It is possible to change this value with the following command in a G-"
"code file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2141
msgid ""
"`#<h_velocity> =` _nn_ - to set the percentage (_nn_) of the current feed "
"rate required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2145
msgid ""
"If Hole Sensing modes 2 or 4 are active, QtPlasmaC will over cut the hole in "
"addition to the velocity changes associated with modes 1 and 3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2148
msgid ""
"The default over cut length for QtPlasmaC hole sensing is 4&#8239;mm "
"(0.157\").  It is possible to change this value with the following command "
"in a G-code file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2150
msgid ""
"`#<oclength> =` _nn_ to specify an over cut length (_nn_) in the same units "
"system as the rest of the G-code file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2154
msgid ""
"This feature can be used in addition to setting the desired hole sensing "
"mode via the appropriate G-code parameter by setting the <<plasma:pause-at-"
"end,Pause At End>> parameter in the MATERIAL frame of the "
"<<plasma:parameters-tab,PARAMETERS Tab>>."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2171
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"G21 (metric)\n"
"G64 P0.005\n"
"M52 P1 (enable adaptive feed)\n"
"F#<_hal[plasmac.cut-feed-rate]> (feed rate from cut parameters)\n"
"#<holes> = 2 (over cut for holes)\n"
"#<oclength> = 6.5 (optional, 6.5 mm over cut length)\n"
"G0 X10 Y10\n"
"M3 $0 S1 (start cut)\n"
"G1 X0\n"
"G3 I10 (the hole)\n"
"M5 $0 (end cut)\n"
"G0 X0 Y0\n"
"M2 (end job)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:2175
msgid ""
"It is OK to have multiple and mixed hole commands in a single G-code file."
msgstr ""

