#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4200
#, fuzzy
msgid "Gouge Speed is 980 mm/min."
msgstr "Fina velocidad de búsqueda de casa en unidades por minuto."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4201
#, fuzzy
msgid "Gouge Distance is 5 mm"
msgstr "Distancia de viaje"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4202
msgid "Creep Speed is 245 mm/min."
msgstr "La velocidad de arrastre es 245 mm/min."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4203
msgid "Creep Distance is 3 mm."
msgstr "Distancia de arrastre es 3 mm."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4205
#, fuzzy
msgid "With this information the following behavior can be described:"
msgstr "Con esta información se pondrá el comando conjunto de esta manera:"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4207
msgid ""
"It is important to note that accelerations and decelerations are omitted "
"from the following calculations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4209
msgid ""
"The torch will start at Pierce Height (4 mm from the material) and start "
"traveling at a Gouge Speed of 980 mm/min (16.3 mm/s) for a Gouge Distance of "
"5 mm which will consume 0.3 seconds (5 mm / 16.3 mm/s = 0.3 s) of the 0.5 s "
"Pierce Motion Delay."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4211
msgid ""
"When the Gouge Distance is reached, the torch speed is set to a Creep Speed "
"of 245 mm/min (4 mm/s) for a Creep Distance of 3 mm. The Creep Distance will "
"take roughly 0.7 seconds to complete (3 mm / 4 mm/s = 0.7 s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4213
msgid ""
"The torch height will remain at 4 mm for another 0.2 seconds (0.5 s (Pierce "
"Motion Delay) - 0.3 s (Gouge Distance at Gouge Speed) = 0.2 s) after which "
"the torch will begin descending to a Pierce End Height of 2.5 mm over the "
"remaining 0.5 seconds of the material's Pierce Delay. Since there are 0.5 "
"seconds of the material's Pierce Delay remaining, as well as 0.5 seconds "
"left at Creep Speed, the Creep Distance will be covered at the same time the "
"Pierce End Height is reached."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4215
msgid ""
"When the Creep Distance has been reached, the torch speed will be set to the "
"material's Cut Feed Rate of 490 mm/min. Since there is a 1 second Cut Height "
"Delay that started at the end of the material's Pierce Delay the transition "
"to a Cut Height of 1.5 mm will occur after the remaining 1 second Cut Height "
"Delay has expired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4217
msgid ""
"The above text should demonstrate that there is quite a bit of configuration "
"and subtlety can be achieved through experimentation and the careful use of "
"different parameter combinations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4221
msgid ""
"It is possible to create translation files for QtPlasmaC to display in the "
"language of the current locale."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4227
msgid ""
"All language files are kept in ~/linuxcnc-dev/share/screens/qtplasmac/"
"languages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4229
msgid ""
"The qtplasmac.py file is a Python version of the GUI file used for "
"translation purposes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4234
msgid "The .qm files are the compiled translation files used by PyQt."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4236
msgid ""
"The directories qtplasmac_4x3/languages and qtplasmac_9x16/languages are "
"only for links to the .qm files in qtplasmac/languages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4240
msgid ""
"The language is determined by an underscore plus the first two letters of "
"the locale.  For example, if an Italian translation was being done then it "
"would be `_it`.  It will be referred to as `_xx` in this document, so "
"`qtplasmac_xx.ts` in this document would actually be `qtplasmac_it.ts` for "
"an Italian translation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4242
msgid ""
"The default locale for QtPlasmaC is `_en` which means that any translation "
"files created as `qtplasmac_en.*` will not be used for translations."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4251
#, no-wrap
msgid "cd ~/linuxcnc-dev/share/qtvcp/screens/qtplasmac/languages\n"
msgstr "cd ~/linuxcnc-dev/share/qtvcp/screens/qtplasmac/languages\n"

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4256
#, no-wrap
msgid "pyuic5 ../qtplasmac.ui > qtplasmac.py\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4261
msgid ""
"The user can either create a new translation source file for a non-existing "
"language translation or modify an existing translation source file due to "
"changes being made to some text in a QtPlasmaC source file.  If modifying an "
"existing translation that has had no source file changes then this step is "
"not required."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4269
msgid ""
"this command is a script which runs the following: $ pylupdate5 *.py ../"
"*.py ../../../../../lib/python/qtvcp/lib/qtplasmac/*.py -ts qtplasmac_xx.ts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4279
msgid ""
"It is not necessary to provide a translation for every text string, if no "
"translation is specified for a string, then the original string will be used "
"in the application.  The user needs to be careful with the length of strings "
"that appear on widgets as space is limited. If possible try, to make the "
"translation no longer than the original."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4287
msgid "Close linguist."
msgstr "Lingüista cercano."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4289
msgid ""
"Then create links to the compiled .qm file for the other QtPlasmaC GUIs."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4291
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ ./langlink xx\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4295
msgid ""
"This command is a script which creates a link in both qtplasmac_4x3/"
"languages and qtplasmac_9x16/languages to the above .qm file and then "
"renames the link to match the GUI name."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4297
msgid ""
"QtPlasmaC will be translated to the language of the current locale on the "
"next start so long as a .qm file exists in that language."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4300
msgid ""
"Users are welcome to submit translation files for inclusion into QtPlasmaC.  "
"An easy method is to post the up to date qtplasmac_xx.ts file on the forum "
"and the maintainers will install the translations."
msgstr ""

#. type: NOTE
#: src/plasma/qtplasmac.adoc:4303
msgid ""
"The preferred method is to submit a pull request from the users GitHub "
"account as described in the https://www.linuxcnc.org/docs/html/code/"
"contributing-to-linuxcnc.html[contributing to LinuxCNC] documentation.  The "
"files required to be committed are qtplasmac_xx.ts and qtplasmac_xx.qm in "
"the qtplasmc/languages directory plus the links in both the qtplasmac_4x3/"
"languages and qtplasmac_9x16/languages directories."
msgstr ""

