#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:95
msgid "B<fault-in> is true"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:107
msgid "B<ok-in> is false"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:110
msgid ""
"To facilitate using only a single fault source, B<ok-in> and B<fault-en> are "
"both set to the non-fault-causing value when no signal is connected\\&. For "
"estop-latch to ever be able to signal a fault, at least one of these inputs "
"must be connected\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:112
msgid ""
"Typically, an external fault or estop input is connected to B<fault-in>, "
"B<iocontrol\\&.0\\&.user-request-enable> is connected to B<reset>, and B<ok-"
"out> is connected to B<iocontrol\\&.0\\&.emc-enable-in>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/estop_latch.9:114
