#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:145
msgid "The desired (commanded) value for the control loop\\&."
msgstr "El valor deseado (ordenado) para el bucle de control\\&."

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:148
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.Pgain> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.Pgain> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:151
msgid ""
"Proportional gain\\&. Results in a contribution to the output that is the "
"error multiplied by B<Pgain>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:154
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.Igain> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.Igain> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:159
msgid ""
"Integral gain\\&. Results in a contribution to the output that is the "
"integral of the error multiplied by B<Igain>\\&. For example an error of "
"0\\&.02 that lasted 10 seconds would result in an integrated error "
"(B<errorI>) of 0\\&.2, and if B<Igain> is 20, the integral term would add "
"4\\&.0 to the output\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:162
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.Dgain> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.Dgain> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:167
msgid ""
"Derivative gain\\&. Results in a contribution to the output that is the rate "
"of change (derivative) of the error multiplied by B<Dgain>\\&. For example "
"an error that changed from 0\\&.02 to 0\\&.03 over 0\\&.2 seconds would "
"result in an error derivative (B<errorD>) of of 0\\&.05, and if B<Dgain> is "
"5, the derivative term would add 0\\&.25 to the output\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:170
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.feedback> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.feedback> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:172
msgid "The actual (feedback) value, from some sensor such as an encoder\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:175
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.output> float out"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.output> float out"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:177
msgid ""
"The output of the PID loop, which goes to some actuator such as a motor\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:180
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.command-deriv> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.command-deriv> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:182
msgid ""
"The derivative of the desired (commanded) value for the control loop\\&. If "
"no signal is connected then the derivative will be estimated numerically\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:185
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.feedback-deriv> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.feedback-deriv> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:187
msgid ""
"The derivative of the actual (feedback) value for the control loop\\&. If no "
"signal is connected then the derivative will be estimated numerically\\&. "
"When the feedback is from a quantized position source (e\\&.g\\&., encoder "
"feedback position), behavior of the D term can be improved by using a better "
"velocity estimate here, such as the velocity output of encoder(9) or "
"hostmot2(9)\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:190
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.error-previous-target> bit in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.error-previous-target> bit in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:192
msgid ""
"Use previous invocation\\(cqs target vs\\&. current position for error "
"calculation, like the motion controller expects\\&. This may make torque-"
"mode position loops and loops requiring a large I gain easier to tune, by "
"eliminating velocity-dependent following error\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:195
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.error> float out"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.error> float out"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:197
msgid "The difference between command and feedback\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:200
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.enable> bit in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.enable> bit in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:204
msgid ""
"When true, enables the PID calculations\\&. When false, B<output> is zero, "
"and all internal integrators, etc, are reset\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:207
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.index-enable> bit in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.index-enable> bit in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:212
msgid ""
"On the falling edge of B<index-enable>, pid does not update the internal "
"command derivative estimate\\&. On systems which use the encoder index "
"pulse, this pin should be connected to the index-enable signal\\&. When this "
"is not done, and FF1 is nonzero, a step change in the input command causes a "
"single-cycle spike in the PID output\\&. On systems which use exactly one of "
"the B<-deriv> inputs, this affects the D term as well\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:215
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.bias> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.bias> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:220
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"B<bias> is a constant amount that is added to the output\\&. In most cases "
"it should be left at zero\\&. However, it can sometimes be useful to "
"compensate for offsets in servo amplifiers, or to balance the weight of an "
"object that moves vertically\\&.  B<bias> is turned off when the PID loop is "
"disabled, just like all other components of the output\\&. If a non-zero "
"output is needed even when the PID loop is disabled, it should be added with "
"an external HAL sum2 block\\&."
msgstr ""
"'BIAS = 0.000' - Esto es utilizado por hm2-servo y algunos otros.  BIAS es "
"una cantidad constante que se agrega a la salida.  En la mayoría de los "
"casos, debe dejarse en cero.  Sin embargo, a veces puede ser útil para "
"compensar servoamplificadores, o para equilibrar el peso de un objeto que se "
"mueve verticalmente. BIAS se desactiva cuando el bucle PID está desactivado, "
"al igual que todos los demás componentes de la salida."

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:223
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF0> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF0> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:229
msgid ""
"Zero order feed-forward term\\&. Produces a contribution to the output that "
"is B<FF0> multiplied by the commanded value\\&. For position loops, it "
"should usually be left at zero\\&. For velocity loops, B<FF0> can compensate "
"for friction or motor counter-EMF and may permit better tuning if used "
"properly\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:232
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF1> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF1> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:236
msgid ""
"First order feed-forward term\\&. Produces a contribution to the output that "
"is B<FF1> multiplied by the derivative of the commanded value\\&. For "
"position loops, the contribution is proportional to speed, and can be used "
"to compensate for friction or motor CEMF\\&. For velocity loops, it is "
"proportional to acceleration and can compensate for inertia\\&. In both "
"cases, it can result in better tuning if used properly\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:239
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF2> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF2> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:243
msgid ""
"Second order feed-forward term\\&. Produces a contribution to the output "
"that is B<FF2> multiplied by the second derivative of the commanded "
"value\\&. For position loops, the contribution is proportional to "
"acceleration, and can be used to compensate for inertia\\&. For velocity "
"loops, the contribution is proportional to jerk, and should usually be left "
"at zero\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:246
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF3> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.FF3> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:250
msgid ""
"Third order feed-forward term\\&. Produces a contribution to the output that "
"is B<FF3> multiplied by the third derivative of the commanded value\\&. For "
"position loops, the contribution is proportional to jerk, and can be used to "
"compensate for residual errors during acceleration\\&. For velocity loops, "
"the contribution is proportional to snap(jounce), and should usually be left "
"at zero\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:253
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.deadband> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.deadband> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:259
msgid ""
"Defines a range of \"acceptable\" error\\&. If the absolute value of "
"B<error> is less than B<deadband>, it will be treated as if the error is "
"zero\\&. When using feedback devices such as encoders that are inherently "
"quantized, the deadband should be set slightly more than one-half count, to "
"prevent the control loop from hunting back and forth if the command is "
"between two adjacent encoder values\\&. When the absolute value of the error "
"is greater than the deadband, the deadband value is subtracted from the "
"error before performing the loop calculations, to prevent a step in the "
"transfer function at the edge of the deadband (see B<BUGS>)\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:262
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxoutput> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxoutput> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:267
msgid ""
"Output limit\\&. The absolute value of the output will not be permitted to "
"exceed B<maxoutput>, unless B<maxoutput> is zero\\&. When the output is "
"limited, the error integrator will hold instead of integrating, to prevent "
"windup and overshoot\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:270
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxerror> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxerror> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:274
msgid ""
"Limit on the internal error variable used for P, I, and D\\&. Can be used to "
"prevent high B<Pgain> values from generating large outputs under conditions "
"when the error is large (for example, when the command makes a step change)"
"\\&. Not normally needed, but can be useful when tuning non-linear "
"systems\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:277
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxerrorD> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxerrorD> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:283
msgid ""
"Limit on the error derivative\\&. The rate of change of error used by the "
"B<Dgain> term will be limited to this value, unless the value is zero\\&. "
"Can be used to limit the effect of B<Dgain> and prevent large output spikes "
"due to steps on the command and/or feedback\\&. Not normally needed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:286
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxerrorI> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxerrorI> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:290
msgid ""
"Limit on error integrator\\&. The error integrator used by the B<Igain> term "
"will be limited to this value, unless it is zero\\&. Can be used to prevent "
"integrator windup and the resulting overshoot during/after sustained "
"errors\\&. Not normally needed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:293
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxcmdD> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxcmdD> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:299
msgid ""
"Limit on command derivative\\&. The command derivative used by B<FF1> will "
"be limited to this value, unless the value is zero\\&. Can be used to "
"prevent B<FF1> from producing large output spikes if there is a step change "
"on the command\\&. Not normally needed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:302
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxcmdDD> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxcmdDD> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:308
msgid ""
"Limit on command second derivative\\&. The command second derivative used by "
"B<FF2> will be limited to this value, unless the value is zero\\&. Can be "
"used to prevent B<FF2> from producing large output spikes if there is a step "
"change on the command\\&. Not normally needed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:311
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxcmdDDD> float in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.maxcmdDDD> float in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:317
msgid ""
"Limit on command third derivative\\&. The command third derivative used by "
"B<FF3> will be limited to this value, unless the value is zero\\&. Can be "
"used to prevent B<FF3> from producing large output spikes if there is a step "
"change on the command\\&. Not normally needed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:320
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.saturated> bit out"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.saturated> bit out"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:322
msgid "When true, the current PID output is saturated\\&. That is,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:326
msgid "B<output> = \\(+- B<maxoutput>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:329
msgid ""
"B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.saturated-s> float out, B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.saturated-"
"count> s32 out"
msgstr ""
"B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.saturated-s> float out, B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.saturated-"
"count> s32 out"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:331
msgid ""
"When true, the output of PID was continually saturated for this many seconds "
"(B<saturated-s>) or periods (B<saturated-count>)\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: man/man9/pid.9:332
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "Additional auto tuning pins"
msgstr "Renombrado de pin adicionales"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:335
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-mode> bit in"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-mode> bit in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:337
msgid ""
"When true, enables auto tune mode\\&. When false, normal PID calculations "
"are performed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:340
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-start> bit io"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-start> bit io"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:342
msgid ""
"When set to true, starts auto tuning\\&. Cleared when the auto tuning "
"completes\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:345
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>*B<\\&.tune-type> u32 rw"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>*B<\\&.tune-type> u32 rw"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:351
msgid ""
"When set to 0, B<Pgain/Igain/Dgain> are calculated\\&. When set to 1, "
"B<Pgain/Igain/FF1> are calculated\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:354
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-cycles> u32 rw"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-cycles> u32 rw"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:358
msgid ""
"Determines the number of cycles to run to characterize the process\\&.  "
"B<tune-cycles> actually sets the number of half cycles\\&. More cycles "
"results in a more accurate characterization as the average of all cycles is "
"used\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:361
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-effort> float rw"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.tune-effort> float rw"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:366
msgid ""
"The maximum output value used during automatic tuning\\&. Determines the "
"effort used in setting up the limit cycle in the process\\&.  B<tune-effort> "
"should be set to a positive value less than B<maxoutput>\\&. Start with "
"something small and work up to a value that results in a good portion of the "
"maximum motor current being used\\&. The smaller the value, the smaller the "
"amplitude of the limit cycle\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:369
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.ultimate-gain> float ro (only if debug=1)"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.ultimate-gain> float ro (solo si debug=1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:375
msgid ""
"Determined from process characterization\\&.  B<ultimate-gain> is the ratio "
"of B<tune-effort> to the limit cycle amplitude multiplied by 4\\&.0 divided "
"by Pi\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:378
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.ultimate-period> float ro (only if debug=1)"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.ultimate-period> float ro (solo si debug=1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:382
msgid ""
"Determined from process characterization\\&.  B<ultimate-period> is the "
"period of the limit cycle\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:386
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.errorI> float ro (only if debug=1)"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.errorI> float ro (solo si debug=1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:390
msgid ""
"Integral of error\\&. This is the value that is multiplied by B<Igain> to "
"produce the Integral term of the output\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:393
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.errorD> float ro (only if debug=1)"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.errorD> float ro (solo si debug=1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:397
msgid ""
"Derivative of error\\&. This is the value that is multiplied by B<Dgain> to "
"produce the Derivative term of the output\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:400
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.commandD> float ro (only if debug=1)"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.commandD> float ro (solo si debug=1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:404
msgid ""
"Derivative of command\\&. This is the value that is multiplied by B<FF1> to "
"produce the first order feed-forward term of the output\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:407
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.commandDD> float ro (only if debug=1)"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.commandDD> float ro (solo si debug=1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:411
msgid ""
"Second derivative of command\\&. This is the value that is multiplied by "
"B<FF2> to produce the second order feed-forward term of the output\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:414
msgid "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.commandDDD> float ro (only if debug=1)"
msgstr "B<pid\\&.>I<N>B<\\&.commandDDD> float ro (solo si debug=1)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:418
msgid ""
"Third derivative of command\\&. This is the value that is multiplied by "
"B<FF3> to produce the third order feed-forward term of the output\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:422
msgid ""
"Some people would argue that deadband should be implemented such that error "
"is treated as zero if it is within the deadband, and be unmodified if it is "
"outside the deadband\\&. This was not done because it would cause a step in "
"the transfer function equal to the size of the deadband\\&. People who "
"prefer that behavior are welcome to add a parameter that will change the "
"behavior, or to write their own version of B<pid>\\&. However, the default "
"behavior should not be changed\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/pid.9:423
msgid ""
"Negative gains may lead to unwanted behavior\\&. It is possible in some "
"situations that negative FF gains make sense, but in general all gains "
"should be positive\\&. If some output is in the wrong direction, negating "
"gains to fix it is a mistake; set the scaling correctly elsewhere instead\\&."
msgstr ""

