#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:38
msgid ""
"This component will control a spindle with adjustable acceleration and "
"deceleration\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"NOTE: This component is unfortunately named and creates pins with names very much like those created by the motion component\\&.\n"
"In nearly every case this is not the documentation page that you are looking for\\&.\n"
"See http://linuxcnc\\&.org/docs/html/man/man9/motion\\&.9\\&.html instead\\&.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:52
msgid ""
"It is designed for use with non-servo spindle drives that have separate fwd/"
"reverse inputs, such as DC drives and inverters\\&. If a spindle encoder is "
"available it is used to tailor the acceleration and deceleration to the "
"spindle load\\&. If not the spindle speed is simulated\\&. The component "
"allows for gearboxes with up to 16 gears\\&. Each gear has individual "
"control of speeds, acceleration, driver gain and direction\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:55
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N> (requires a floating-point thread)"
msgstr "B<spindle>\\&.I<N> (requiere un hilo de punto flotante)"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:60
msgid "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<select-gear> u32 in"
msgstr "B<spindle>\\&.I<N>\\&.B<select-gear> u32 in"

#. type: Plain text
#: man/man9/spindle.9:62
msgid ""
"Select a gear\\&. Must be in the range 0 → number of available gears -1\\&. "
"If you use this, do not use the select\\&.x input pins\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
